Subject: [PATCH] core: widen 5-bit colour to 8 bits by table, not by divide

bgra() converts a SNES BGR555 colour to the 32-bit "BGRA" buffer the public
API exposes. It does three 32-bit multiplies and three integer divides per
pixel, over 256x239 = 61184 pixels, every frame:

    uint32_t blue  = (color & 31u)         * 255u / 31u;
    uint32_t green = ((color >> 5) & 31u)  * 255u / 31u;
    uint32_t red   = ((color >> 10) & 31u) * 255u / 31u;

The 3DS ARM11 has no fast integer divide. Profiling the running port put the
frame-conversion call at roughly half of simcity_recomp_advance(), and
advance() at 91% of the main loop, while the core reported only ~12 281 guest
instructions per frame, which cannot account for it. The cost is host-side work
the instruction counter does not cover.

The obvious replacement, (v<<3)|(v>>2), is WRONG. That is the 5->5->8 widening
and it is not (v*255)/31: it diverges on 15 of the 32 inputs (v=4 -> 33 vs 32,
v=16 -> 132 vs 131, v=30 -> 247 vs 246). Applying it would shift 15 tones of
every palette. It was caught by testing all 32 values before sending anything.

What is exact is a 32-entry lookup indexed by the 5-bit channel: a byte load
per channel, no multiply, no divide, and bit-identical output. Verified for
all 32768 BGR555 words end to end, old versus new.

This changes no output value. If it does not move the frame rate, the divides
are not the wall, and the remaining cost is elsewhere - in which case do not
proceed with the RGB565 plan on the strength of this change.

--- a/src/sc_v28_video.c	2026-10-17 12:48:24.887615763 +0100
+++ b/src/sc_v28_video.c	2026-10-17 12:48:24.948616298 +0100
@@ -110,12 +110,24 @@
            ((uint16_t)g_cgram[address + 1u] << 8)) & 0x7fffu;
 }
 
+/* Widen a 5-bit channel to 8 bits, exactly reproducing (v*255)/31 without the
+ * multiply and the divide. One byte load per channel.
+ *
+ * NOT (v<<3)|(v>>2): that is the 5->5->8 widening and differs from the divide
+ * on 15 of 32 inputs (v=4 -> 33 vs 32, v=16 -> 132 vs 131). Verified equal to
+ * (v*255)/31 for all v in 0..31, and for all 32768 BGR555 words end to end. */
+static const uint8_t widen5[32] = {
+     0,   8,  16,  24,  32,  41,  49,  57,  65,  74,  82,  90,  98, 106,
+   115, 123, 131, 139, 148, 156, 164, 172, 180, 189, 197, 205, 213, 222,
+   230, 238, 246, 255
+};
+
 static uint32_t bgra(uint16_t color) {
     /* SNES CGRAM stores colors in BGR555 format:
      * bits 0-4 = Blue, bits 5-9 = Green, bits 10-14 = Red */
-    uint32_t blue = (color & 31u) * 255u / 31u;
-    uint32_t green = ((color >> 5) & 31u) * 255u / 31u;
-    uint32_t red = ((color >> 10) & 31u) * 255u / 31u;
+    uint32_t blue = widen5[color & 31u];
+    uint32_t green = widen5[(color >> 5) & 31u];
+    uint32_t red = widen5[(color >> 10) & 31u];
     return 0xFF000000u | (blue) | (green << 8) | (red << 16);
 }
 
